# Keep the aos-bench build context (`COPY . /opt/aos`) small. Without
# this, the context streams the whole repo (tens of GB — dominated by a
# 3.5 GB crates/target Rust artifact dir, a large .claude agent-worktree
# dir, .git, and build outputs), which makes the build take 20+ min on
# macOS Docker and bloats the image.
#
# Mirrors .gitignore: everything here is a build artifact / cache /
# local-only path that the Nix flake never reads. NOTE we deliberately
# keep crates/ itself (the vendored Rust *sources* under crates/<name>/)
# because flake.nix references ./crates during `pkgPackages` /
# `systemPackages` enumeration — dropping the whole dir makes even a
# pure-C target like pkg-zlib fail eval with "path '.../crates' does not
# exist". Only the generated crates/target/ (3.5 GB) is excluded.
#
# Anchored (leading /) where root-only so BuildKit doesn't walk pruned
# subtrees (the documented unanchored-negation cost); the **/target and
# cache patterns intentionally match at any depth.
/.claude
/.git
/.direnv
/.idea
/.jj

# Built images, QEMU artifacts, cached tarballs, Nix results (gitignored)
/output
/mirror
/result
result-*

# Rust build artifacts — the bulk of the context (gitignored). Keep the
# crate sources, drop only the compiled target trees.
crates/target/
cli/target/

# Python + doc caches (gitignored)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.aos-doc-cache.json

# Per-operator ignition config (gitignored; bakes in an SSH key)
/tests/ignition-test.json
